WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.078
Someone once said that the best way

00:00:02.078 --> 00:00:05.202
to learn about a city is
to leave your hotel room

00:00:05.202 --> 00:00:06.884
and meet the locals.

00:00:06.884 --> 00:00:09.244
You guys have been friends for how long?

00:00:09.244 --> 00:00:10.985
Couple years?
Yeah.

00:00:10.985 --> 00:00:12.673
How do you refer to each other?

00:00:12.673 --> 00:00:14.048
If you're two Australians

00:00:14.048 --> 00:00:14.881
do you just say

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:15.714
hey, mate?

00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:17.156
Or you can add O on the end of their name.

00:00:17.156 --> 00:00:18.798
So, you could be.

00:00:18.798 --> 00:00:19.631
He's Jonathan,

00:00:19.631 --> 00:00:20.464
becomes John-o.

00:00:20.464 --> 00:00:21.297
Johno.

00:00:21.297 --> 00:00:22.130
And what's your name?

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:22.963
Jim becomes Jim-o.

00:00:22.963 --> 00:00:24.344
Jimo, would I be Conan-o?

00:00:24.344 --> 00:00:25.217
Oh yeah, Con-o.

00:00:25.217 --> 00:00:26.050
I'd be Con-o.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:27.429
If you're Gary, it's Gaz-o.

00:00:27.429 --> 00:00:28.834
All right, I'm gonna do something.

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:30.309
I'm gonna sit down and pretend we're

00:00:30.309 --> 00:00:31.742
all three really good mates

00:00:31.742 --> 00:00:33.841
that have known each other for four years.

00:00:33.841 --> 00:00:35.363
I'm Con-o.

00:00:35.363 --> 00:00:36.220
John-o.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.153
Jim-o.

00:00:37.153 --> 00:00:37.986
And let's just talk,

00:00:37.986 --> 00:00:40.068
and use as much Australian
slang as you can.

00:00:40.068 --> 00:00:40.901
Okay?

00:00:40.901 --> 00:00:43.192
We'll try our best.

00:00:43.192 --> 00:00:44.025
Hey!

00:00:44.025 --> 00:00:44.858
Hey, Conan.

00:00:44.858 --> 00:00:45.964
Hey!

00:00:45.964 --> 00:00:47.255
Sorry!

00:00:47.255 --> 00:00:48.238
What the hell was that?

00:00:48.238 --> 00:00:49.096
No!

00:00:49.096 --> 00:00:50.860
We're gonna keep that in.
This is my first time on TV.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:51.693
John-o.

00:00:51.693 --> 00:00:52.826
John-o.
Jim-o.

00:00:52.826 --> 00:00:54.492
Jim-o and Con-o.
Con-O.

00:00:54.492 --> 00:00:55.325
Do you think you got that this time?

00:00:55.325 --> 00:00:56.701
I got it this time.

00:00:56.701 --> 00:00:58.081
Hey, John-o!

00:00:58.081 --> 00:00:58.914
Con-o!

00:00:58.914 --> 00:00:59.747
Hey!
Nice to meet you.

00:00:59.747 --> 00:01:00.580
Con-o.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:01.413
Did you say nice to meet you?

00:01:01.413 --> 00:01:02.246
Yeah.

00:01:02.246 --> 00:01:03.530
No, we've been friends for years!

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.901
(laughing)

00:01:04.901 --> 00:01:07.854
I said we've been friends for.

00:01:07.854 --> 00:01:08.687
What is with him?

00:01:08.687 --> 00:01:09.645
What's with John-o?

00:01:09.645 --> 00:01:10.478
Listen.
We just need

00:01:10.478 --> 00:01:11.427
to warm up to you.
We have been friends

00:01:11.427 --> 00:01:12.260
for years.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:13.285
We share a flat together.

00:01:13.285 --> 00:01:14.179
Been ages, you're right.

00:01:14.179 --> 00:01:16.584
It's been ages, we've done it all.

00:01:16.584 --> 00:01:18.772
Okay, we've done it all.

00:01:18.772 --> 00:01:19.605
Okay?
(laughs)

00:01:19.605 --> 00:01:21.262
I've been in jail for a little bit.

00:01:21.262 --> 00:01:22.095
Okay?

00:01:22.095 --> 00:01:23.349
And we don't wanna talk about what I did.

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:24.182
Right.

00:01:24.182 --> 00:01:25.015
I don't think I really did it,

00:01:25.015 --> 00:01:26.537
but they say I did.

00:01:26.537 --> 00:01:28.128
Here we go.

00:01:28.128 --> 00:01:29.820
(laughing)

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:30.936
Hey, John-o!

00:01:30.936 --> 00:01:32.593
Con-o, how are you doing?
Hey!

00:01:32.593 --> 00:01:33.574
How was Long Bay?

00:01:33.574 --> 00:01:35.416
Oh, Long Bays!

00:01:35.416 --> 00:01:38.077
Oh mate, how lucky are we?

00:01:38.077 --> 00:01:39.065
Huh?

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:40.040
You didn't have a surf recently?

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:41.338
Ah, surf.

00:01:41.338 --> 00:01:42.178
Oh, yeah.

00:01:42.178 --> 00:01:43.816
Good on ya.

00:01:43.816 --> 00:01:45.243
(laughing)

00:01:45.243 --> 00:01:46.524
Did you ride any barrels down there?

00:01:46.524 --> 00:01:47.746
Oh, barrels!

00:01:47.746 --> 00:01:50.634
(laughing)

00:01:50.634 --> 00:01:52.186
Oh, yeah, yeah.

00:01:52.186 --> 00:01:53.403
You get out through the barrel and--

00:01:53.403 --> 00:01:54.912
Barrels, right through the barrels.

00:01:54.912 --> 00:01:56.525
before you know it, you're in a billabong.

00:01:56.525 --> 00:01:58.005
Um-de-bumbdy-billabong.

00:01:58.005 --> 00:01:59.526
Um-de-bumbdy-billabong!

00:01:59.526 --> 00:02:00.743
Suddenly, I'm a man at work

00:02:00.743 --> 00:02:03.432
and then over there you got, you know.

00:02:03.432 --> 00:02:04.398
Land down under,

00:02:04.398 --> 00:02:05.388
that's what it's like.
Yeah, exactly!

00:02:05.388 --> 00:02:06.221
But fair dinkum.

00:02:06.221 --> 00:02:07.822
But hey, John-O!

00:02:07.822 --> 00:02:09.108
You're a little mumsy with the tumsy.

00:02:09.108 --> 00:02:09.941
